From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 08:45:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 014/190] segacd: add a headless console soak for reproducing
 display bugs

Heavy console output is the one screen the desktop never exercises: an
all-background page with text on it. Driving EmuDesk's "Show file" from
a script means steering the mouse pointer through two double-clicks,
which is fragile; this prints a text page from biosmain instead, before
the desktop starts, so the case reproduces under the emulators with no
input at all.

Off unless CONF_SEGACD_CONSOLE_SOAK is defined as the number of lines:

  make segacd ELF=1 DEF='-DCONF_SEGACD_CONSOLE_SOAK=12'

This is what found the plane-B transparency bug the servant had.
---
 bios/bios.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bios/bios.c b/bios/bios.c
index 48dfc0a..316623b 100644
--- a/bios/bios.c
+++ b/bios/bios.c
@@ -873,6 +873,23 @@ void biosmain(void)
     }
 #endif
 
+#if defined(MACHINE_SEGACD) && defined(CONF_SEGACD_CONSOLE_SOAK)
+    /*
+     * Diagnostic build only: hammer the VT52 console the way EmuDesk's
+     * "Show file" and EmuCON do, with no input needed, so the hardware
+     * text-smear bug can be reproduced headlessly under the emulators.
+     */
+    {
+        int i;
+        cprintf("\033E");               /* clear screen, like show_file() */
+        for (i = 0; i < CONF_SEGACD_CONSOLE_SOAK; i++)
+            cprintf("EmuTOS console soak %02d ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ\r\n",
+                    i & 0xff);
+        for (;;)                        /* freeze with the text on screen */
+            ;
+    }
+#endif
+
     autoexec();                 /* autoexec PRGs from AUTO folder */
 
     /* clear commandline */
